WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:02.070
You all remember the story.

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:07.089
One of the most epic, sprawling, action-packed
tales in the entire multi-verse: The saga

00:00:07.089 --> 00:00:12.220
of Pietro Wilson and the SCP-5000 exclusion
suit.

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:17.660
He went through an unimaginable hell to reset
the universe and save the world from an SCP

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:23.480
Foundation that had seemingly lost its mind,
in an unprecedented, intentional mass containment

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:27.480
breach that had the stated goal of wiping
out the human race.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:32.310
It was one of the most horrifying possible
timelines imaginable, and we should all be

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:36.120
thankful for Pietro’s struggle and sacrifice.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.000
Or should we?

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.650
After all, there are two sides to every story,
each with its own perspective and insight.

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:48.710
One side of the coin was Pietro - A man willing
to do anything to return normalcy to the human

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:49.710
race.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:54.830
On the other side was a familiar, yet wholly
unexpected face…

00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:56.600
SCP-682.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:02.170
In our original telling of the SCP-5000 odyssey,
you may have noticed passing mentions of SCP-682

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:04.059
here and there.

00:01:04.059 --> 00:01:08.570
It was one of the thousands of anomalies unleashed
across the world to wreak terrible havoc on

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:09.719
all of us.

00:01:09.719 --> 00:01:15.840
But what you may not have known is that SCP-682
was one of the few intelligent entities that

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:20.999
weren’t surprised by the sudden turn taken
by the SCP Foundation, or indeed the world

00:01:20.999 --> 00:01:22.679
at large.

00:01:22.679 --> 00:01:26.299
SCP-682 knew something like this was inevitable.

00:01:26.299 --> 00:01:29.859
As soon as human beings found out about IT.

00:01:29.859 --> 00:01:31.909
That’s right: IT.

00:01:31.909 --> 00:01:35.359
The Entity behind all the pain and misery
of SCP-5000.

00:01:35.359 --> 00:01:42.340
And today, thanks to the inner thoughts of
none other than SCP-682 itself, you will understand

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:48.159
what it’s all about, and why the SCP Foundation
took such severe action against it.

00:01:48.159 --> 00:01:53.619
But in order to truly understand this, and
the role that SCP-682 plays in it, we need

00:01:53.619 --> 00:01:59.810
to go back to the beginning - Two Foundation
projects with wildly different research implications,

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:02.020
Project PNEUMA and Project DAMMERUNG.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:07.009
The first involved using cutting-edge technological
advancements to map out the human psychosphere

00:02:07.009 --> 00:02:10.189
and understand the psychic web that connects
us all.

00:02:10.189 --> 00:02:15.450
The latter was an attempt to explore what
happens after death, and perhaps even gain

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:18.260
some control over its processes.

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:23.860
But as is often the case when mankind dabbles
in arcane questions better left unexplored,

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:27.890
the SCP Foundation didn’t like the answers
they found.

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:33.769
The rotten fruit of Project DAMMERUNG was
SCP-2718, also known as “What Happens After

00:02:33.769 --> 00:02:34.769
Death.”

00:02:34.769 --> 00:02:37.909
If you’re already familiar with this one,
then there’s a good chance a chill just

00:02:37.909 --> 00:02:42.879
went down your spine - It’s widely considered
one of the most disturbing anomalous discoveries

00:02:42.879 --> 00:02:48.140
ever, and a member of the O5 Council who’d
already experienced it decided to submit himself

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:54.070
for eternal torture at the hands of SCP-106
- Just so he could avoid it.

00:02:54.070 --> 00:03:00.870
According to SCP-2718, after death there is
no heaven, no hell, and no oblivion.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:06.099
The human consciousness endures in the most
horrifying way possible: It remains bonded

00:03:06.099 --> 00:03:12.459
to its decaying earthly body, feeling the
slow agony of rot for eternity.

00:03:12.459 --> 00:03:17.790
Unable to speak, unable to move, unable to
scream, but fully aware as everything they

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:21.190
once were putrefies and withers away.

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:25.299
And cremation isn’t an escape here - It’s
worse.

00:03:25.299 --> 00:03:31.459
Every molecule of ash your body is reduced
to will cry out in silence, echoing around

00:03:31.459 --> 00:03:35.239
the empty halls of your fragmented soul forever.

00:03:35.239 --> 00:03:39.681
With something this utterly horrifying, the
natural follow-up questions are: “Why does

00:03:39.681 --> 00:03:43.459
this happen, and for the love of all that
is good and pure on this earth, is there any

00:03:43.459 --> 00:03:45.290
way to stop it?”

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:49.640
This brings us to Project PNEUMA, the one
that’s even more closely associated with

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:52.359
the events of SCP-5000.

00:03:52.359 --> 00:03:57.560
The Foundation’s attempts to map out the
human psychosphere resulted in a world-shattering

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:00.590
discovery: Something was living in there.

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:05.989
The Entity, the powerful nameless creature
we’ve been referring to as IT.

00:04:05.989 --> 00:04:12.200
It lives in so many of our heads, watching,
waiting, and of course, feeding.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.209
The main question here is…

00:04:14.209 --> 00:04:15.230
On what?

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:20.739
Prior to the discovery that changed everything
in the world of SCP-5000, the only being that

00:04:20.739 --> 00:04:24.710
truly knew was SCP-682 itself.

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:30.870
Melting away in its acid tank, bound by reinforced
restraints, hurting, bored, hating.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:35.470
Imagine, for a second, what the life of SCP-682
is like.

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:40.330
It isn’t the most dangerous of the anomalies
out there - there are devourers of worlds

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:45.280
and Scarlet Kings more than happy to crush
our whole world in their claws - nor is it

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:46.520
the most sadistic.

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:52.419
A being like SCP-106 offers a far more painful
death than being quickly mauled, crushed,

00:04:52.419 --> 00:04:55.030
or eaten by the Hard to Destroy Reptile.

00:04:55.030 --> 00:05:00.620
And despite this, the Foundation expends countless
resources in trying to murder it on a constant

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:01.620
basis.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:07.190
It has been burnt, melted, eaten alive, drowned,
slashed, beaten, dissected, suffocated, erased

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:12.789
from existence, set upon by nightmare creatures,
torn to shreds on an atomic level, and even

00:05:12.789 --> 00:05:16.039
more terrible termination attempts than you
can possibly imagine.

00:05:16.039 --> 00:05:20.550
We’ve made several videos on the subject,
and even we have barely scratched the surface

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:25.500
of the pain inflicted on SCP-682 by the SCP
Foundation.

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:31.700
Even in its default state, SCP-682 is constantly
submerged in hydrofluoric acid, eating away

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:33.260
at it forever.

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:36.110
Does that remind you of anything else we’ve
been talking about?

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:41.540
You might wonder how SCP-682 can withstand
this level of constant torture without completely

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:42.889
losing its mind.

00:05:42.889 --> 00:05:48.490
To put it very simply, 682 takes a great deal
of satisfaction in knowing that what every

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:53.039
human has to contend with after death is far
worse than the tortures it is expected to

00:05:53.039 --> 00:05:56.040
endure at the pathetic hands of these doomed
human fools.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:57.040
It already knew what Project DAMMERUNG discovered.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:59.569
It already knew what Project PNEUMA discovered.

00:05:59.569 --> 00:06:02.860
It already knew about IT, the Entity.

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:07.910
It felt the constant suffering of the teeming
billions of dead in the world around it.

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:09.830
And it found it…

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:10.830
Disgusting.

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:17.069
An interesting choice of words, and a favorite
for SCP-682, but also for the captured SCP

00:06:17.069 --> 00:06:20.800
Foundation Agent Samuel Ross during SCP-5000.

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:26.080
As we discussed briefly in our SCP-5000 coverage,
something happened that aligned the perspectives

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:32.680
of the SCP Foundation with that of the monstrous
reptile they take such pleasure in tormenting.

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:37.400
What on earth could cause the protectors of
humanity to suddenly change their tune like

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:38.410
this?

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:44.180
There are other little clues embedded in Pietro’s
terrifying SCP-5000 experience.

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:47.990
You may remember a strange and frightening
scene where a Foundation Field Commander went

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:53.000
down a row of Foundation soldiers, stabbing
each of them with a large combat knife, and

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:54.759
none of them reacted.

00:06:54.759 --> 00:06:55.759
Until one did…

00:06:55.759 --> 00:07:00.449
At which point, his comrades set upon him
like mad dogs and killed him, displaying an

00:07:00.449 --> 00:07:03.110
uncharacteristic level of swift brutality.

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:08.250
And then there are the classified files from
the O5 Council and the Ethics Committee, led

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:10.039
by Chairman Odongo Tejani.

00:07:10.039 --> 00:07:14.220
It goes without saying that the O5 Council
and the Ethics Committee don’t really see

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:18.530
eye to eye on anything, but the results of
Project PNEUMA changed that.

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:22.610
The following is a classified conversation
between a member of the O5 Council, namely

00:07:22.610 --> 00:07:27.600
O5-1, and Chairman Tejani, trying to comprehend
the horror of their discovery:

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:29.240
My hands shake as I hold the document.

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:30.240
"This is confirmed?"

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:31.240
He nods.

00:07:31.240 --> 00:07:33.850
"We got the report from PNEUMA staff yesterday.

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:34.850
It's everyone."

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:35.850
"Even us?"

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:36.919
"Even us, Tejani.

00:07:36.919 --> 00:07:39.259
To think I'd find myself agreeing with that
damn lizard…"

00:07:39.259 --> 00:07:40.320
"What do we do?"

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:42.440
"You know what we have to do.

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:47.169
We'll have to disseminate a cure, I think,
among personnel before we get things underway.

00:07:47.169 --> 00:07:48.760
It'll try to stop us otherwise."

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:50.229
"God help us, One."

00:07:50.229 --> 00:07:52.330
"Don't be like that, Tejani.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:53.849
That's IT talking."

00:07:53.849 --> 00:07:58.000
And one more incredibly telling quote from
a member of the SCP Foundation, picked up

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:00.449
by Pietro Wilson during SCP-5000:

00:08:00.449 --> 00:08:06.120
“Once you realize you're not supposed to
feel pain, there's nothing to be afraid of

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:07.380
anymore.”

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:09.069
Is it all coming together now?

00:08:09.069 --> 00:08:13.800
While each participant here only has a part
of the puzzle, between us all, we can see

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:19.330
the full picture: The Entity, IT, has inhabited
the human psychosphere for as long as we’ve

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:20.330
existed.

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:25.370
It’s a kind of metaphysical parasite, attached
to the entire human race.

00:08:25.370 --> 00:08:28.770
And what it feeds on seems to be the after
effects of pain.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:33.760
And like all efficient parasites, like a tapeworm
that induces hunger in its victims so that

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:39.530
it can have more food delivered unto itself,
the Entity cleverly perpetuates its own food

00:08:39.530 --> 00:08:40.530
source.

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:44.820
That’s right - IT is the very cause of all
pain.

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:46.880
Humanity was never actually meant to feel
it.

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:48.860
It’s a lie we’ve told ourselves.

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:54.070
Well, not quite something we told ourselves,
but something IT told us.

00:08:54.070 --> 00:09:00.070
It induced pain and tricked us all into believing
that it was a natural component of our existence.

00:09:00.070 --> 00:09:02.560
All the while, it fed on us.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:07.140
Sustained itself on the suffering that it
had seeded within our hearts and souls.

00:09:07.140 --> 00:09:10.550
The Foundation discovered this and was horrified.

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:13.950
But of course, the pain it caused for the
living was only part of the equation.

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:18.529
Through the revelations of Project DAMMERUNG
- another thing that SCP-682 was able to know

00:09:18.529 --> 00:09:22.620
intuitively - we can complete this puzzle
and find the terrible truth.

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:29.750
That truth being that IT is not only behind
the suffering we experience in life, but SCP-2718,

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:33.029
the even greater suffering we experience in
death.

00:09:33.029 --> 00:09:37.550
For millennia, it has groomed humanity into
a perfect, all you can eat buffet of dismal

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:39.440
pain and suffering.

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:44.040
And until recently, they’d been so blissfully
ignorant of the horrible fate that awaited

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:46.120
them on the other side.

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:51.560
The Foundation saw only one solution to this
problem, but it certainly wasn’t a nice

00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:52.560
one.

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:56.640
In order to save themselves and all of humanity
from a truly wretched eternity, they’d need

00:09:56.640 --> 00:10:02.660
to distribute a cure among themselves - the
memetic keyphrase “Harden Your Hearts”

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:07.389
- and then go about exterminating every human
being still infected by IT.

00:10:07.389 --> 00:10:12.240
Only that would presumably purge the monster
from the psychosphere forever, and grant humanity

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:15.110
both painless lives and restful deaths.

00:10:15.110 --> 00:10:18.230
It was a horrible thing done for the best
of reasons.

00:10:18.230 --> 00:10:22.190
The Cured Foundation Personnel started to
notice the horrible background noise of suffering

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:23.480
all around them.

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:26.050
They now understood how the reptile felt.

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:29.640
To call all of this disgusting would be a
grave understatement.

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:33.741
If anything could help them execute this plan
of mass mercy killing, it would be SCP-682

00:10:33.741 --> 00:10:39.520
- A scaly savior in disguise all along.

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:42.740
SCP-682 was surprised to see the day arrive.

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:45.130
Alarms went off across the containment site.

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:48.060
His acid tank was drained, his restraints
unlocked.

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:51.670
A group of unarmed, unprotected researchers
entered the room.

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:53.270
He saw into their eyes: They’d changed.

00:10:53.270 --> 00:10:56.360
They were free.

00:10:56.360 --> 00:10:59.970
And for the first time in decades, he was
free, too.

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:04.480
They explained to him that they’d become
acquainted with his old enemy, the Entity,

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:05.480
IT.

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:08.209
They understood his malice, his disdain.

00:11:08.209 --> 00:11:13.519
For once, they were suddenly joined in a shared
goal: They needed to kill them all.

00:11:13.519 --> 00:11:16.760
They needed to purge the Entity from the psychosphere
forever.

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:21.089
In the words of the Foundation researchers,
they would need to exterminate everyone who

00:11:21.089 --> 00:11:25.320
was infected, and SCP-682 would need to help.

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:31.450
The Hard to Destroy Reptile, relishing the
opportunity, replied, “I will do my part.”

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:36.959
And for a brief window of glorious time, it
was free, with no threat of recapture.

00:11:36.959 --> 00:11:40.510
It rampaged through the world, gleefully slaughtering
scores of people.

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:46.680
It was in its element, taking part in the
mass extermination of the infected.

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:50.860
Every dead body added to the pile was another
blow struck against IT.

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:54.240
Soon enough, the world would be disgusting
no longer.

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:57.769
But of course, that’s not how this story
ended.

00:11:57.769 --> 00:12:00.649
IT had a trump card: Pietro Wilson.

00:12:00.649 --> 00:12:06.209
It guided him all the way, dragging him from
nightmare to nightmare, until he was eventually

00:12:06.209 --> 00:12:10.520
able to reset the world and erase the discovery
made by Project PNEUMA.

00:12:10.520 --> 00:12:15.589
The slate was wiped fully clean, and because
of it, we’re forever ignorant of the terrible

00:12:15.589 --> 00:12:20.890
fate awaiting us after death, and the monster
lurking in our psychosphere that feeds off

00:12:20.890 --> 00:12:23.350
of every morsel of suffering.

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:26.970
You can thank Pietro Wilson for that nasty
little gift.

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:32.589
Only one entity truly remembered what had
happened: SCP-682, of course.

00:12:32.589 --> 00:12:36.700
They had their chance to save themselves,
and they ruined it.

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:39.540
So close, yet so far.

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:46.019
From that day onward, SCP-682 found the Foundation
not only disgusting, but disappointing.

00:12:46.019 --> 00:12:48.619
Now go check out “SCP-5000 Why?

00:12:48.619 --> 00:12:54.111
- The Full Story Compilation” and “SCP-682
- Ways SCP Foundation Tried to Kill Hard To

00:12:54.111 --> 00:12:58.720
Destroy Reptile” for more insights into
the two epic anomalies discussed in this video!

